{"title":"2016 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 13","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(no_casework)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (no casework)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Five friends sat in a movie theater in a row containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> seats, numbered <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> from left to right. (The directions \"left\" and \"right\" are from the point of view of the people as they sit in the seats.) During the movie Ada went to the lobby to get some popcorn. When she returned, she found that Bea had moved two seats to the right, Ceci had moved one seat to the left, and Dee and Edie had switched seats, leaving an end seat for Ada. In which seat had Ada been sitting before she got up?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f50921f19c1ff41715425e558809deff27eea31c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }1 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 3 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 4\\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"353\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Assume that Edie and Dee were originally in seats 3 and 4. If this were so, there is no possible position for which Bea can move 2 seats to the right. The same applies for seats 2 and 3. Also, if Edie and Dee were in seats 2 and 4, Ceci would have nowhere to go. This means that either Edie or Dee was originally in an edge seat. If Edie and Dee were in seats 1 and 2, then Bea must have been in seat 3, which would mean that seat 5 would now be occupied and the positioning would not work. So, Edie and Dee are in seats 4 and 5. This means that Bea was originally in seat 1. Ceci must have been in seat 3 to keep seat 1 open, which leaves seat 2.\n</p><p>Thus, Ada was in seat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/e/9fee36265d80f955ca6b0c0efb730384788a1861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B) }2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the person (out of A,B,C) that moves the most, moves the amount equal to the sum of what the other 2 move. They essentially make a cycle. D &amp; E are seat fillers and can be ignored. A,B,C take up either seats 1,2,3 or 2,4,5. In each case you find A was originally in seat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e8656291085c388b48a0fa8da85aed21c483bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28no_casework.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(no_casework)\">Solution 3 (no casework)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (no casework)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note that the net displacements in the right direction sum up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. The sum of the net displacements of Bea, Ceci, Dee, Edie is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/4/5a47fb988162ee537bf90d7d4721bef5cc57f264.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2-1 = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" />, so Ada moved exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> place to the left. Since Ada ended on an end seat, she must have started on seat <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/e/b5e8656291085c388b48a0fa8da85aed21c483bf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"20\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.28CREATIVE_THINKING.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_(CREATIVE_THINKING)\">Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution (CREATIVE THINKING)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/YPz72EyJzbw\">https://youtu.be/YPz72EyJzbw</a>\n</p><p>~Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/dHY8gjoYFXU?t=664\">https://youtu.be/dHY8gjoYFXU?t=664</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/wKfU1CF-HaA\">https://youtu.be/wKfU1CF-HaA</a>\n</p><p>~savannahsolver\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_13&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A\" title=\"2016 AMC 10A\">2016 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2016 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2016 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2016 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 12\">Problem 12</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2016 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2016 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2016 AMC 10A Problems/Pro